1
00:00:02,070 --> 00:00:04,950
This cocoa pod is weeks from harvest.

2
00:00:05,673 --> 00:00:07,483
Then the rain comes.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,705
With the rain comes a disease:

4
00:00:10,745 --> 00:00:11,743
black pod.

5
00:00:11,783 --> 00:00:14,255
Each drop that splashes off an infected

6
00:00:14,295 --> 00:00:17,203
pod can carry the disease to the next.

7
00:00:17,243 --> 00:00:19,455
Worldwide, it destroys an estimated

8
00:00:19,495 --> 00:00:22,896
twenty to thirty percent of cocoa, every year.

9
00:00:23,595 --> 00:00:24,651
In Malaysia,

10
00:00:24,691 --> 00:00:27,564
most cocoa grows on small farms like this one.

11
00:00:27,604 --> 00:00:29,875
After a storm, this farmer has a golden

12
00:00:29,915 --> 00:00:32,069
half-hour to check eight blocks.

13
00:00:32,109 --> 00:00:33,399
But where should he start?

14
00:00:36,613 --> 00:00:38,908
KokoShield watches the rain for him.

15
00:00:38,948 --> 00:00:41,537
Last night, forty-eight millimetres fell,

16
00:00:41,577 --> 00:00:43,401
well past its alarm level.

17
00:00:43,441 --> 00:00:44,636
Time to search.

18
00:00:45,181 --> 00:00:47,217
To pick where, it gathers clues.

19
00:00:47,257 --> 00:00:48,655
A borrowed drone shows

20
00:00:48,695 --> 00:00:50,519
where water still stands.

21
00:00:50,559 --> 00:00:52,700
A small 3D-printed sensor

22
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:55,012
measures how damp the air is.

23
00:00:55,052 --> 00:00:57,606
Add the rain gauge and past outbreaks,

24
00:00:57,646 --> 00:00:59,950
and every block gets a score.

25
00:01:00,568 --> 00:01:02,957
In seconds, he has a thirty-minute plan:

26
00:01:02,997 --> 00:01:06,882
block A first, then D, B and G.

27
00:01:07,410 --> 00:01:08,278
He heads out.

28
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:10,401
His phone shows what to look for at each stop,

29
00:01:10,441 --> 00:01:11,660
even offline.

30
00:01:12,297 --> 00:01:15,288
Two minutes in, at block A, he spots it:

31
00:01:15,328 --> 00:01:17,340
dark patches on the lower pods.

32
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:20,722
He snaps a photo, and an adviser confirms it.

33
00:01:21,545 --> 00:01:23,062
But does the plan really help?

34
00:01:23,102 --> 00:01:24,711
Let's test both routes.

35
00:01:28,930 --> 00:01:31,768
His usual route finds two infected pods,

36
00:01:31,808 --> 00:01:34,350
and walks right past two sick blocks.

37
00:01:34,390 --> 00:01:36,461
KokoShield's route finds seven,

38
00:01:36,501 --> 00:01:37,697
and misses none.

39
00:01:38,927 --> 00:01:40,703
Every pod caught early can be

40
00:01:40,743 --> 00:01:42,531
removed before it spreads.

41
00:01:42,571 --> 00:01:44,842
That means less cocoa lost, and steadier

42
00:01:44,882 --> 00:01:46,729
income for the families who grow it.

43
00:01:46,769 --> 00:01:48,403
We're in talks with a cocoa farm

44
00:01:48,443 --> 00:01:50,962
in Tanjung Sepat for the first pilot,

45
00:01:51,002 --> 00:01:52,955
on a budget of twelve hundred ringgit.
